{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789515045,"nonce":"zO7oIEc0br088yoDJoHVyX7DQ9A=","title":"Python: a store into a field only ever given None was stored as None","message":"A field whose every write in view is None (`self.pending = None`) had the type None, and a value stored into it through a dynamic receiver (`d.pending = pkt` with `d` dynamic) was coerced to None: the store wrote null and the program went on with a wrong state (richards' device task never saw its packet). Two changes: an attribute store through a dynamic receiver widens the field on every class that has one, and through a receiver of a known class widens that class's field, so the type is right; and the dynamic store into a field that is still None-typed raises TypeError instead of storing None.","files":null}]}